{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler orchestrator) assigned task #5317: \"[stitch] cmd/sha512sum completion (srd033 R3.2, R4.1, R4.2, R4.3)\". The task requires:\n   - Finalizing cmd/sha512sum/main.go to ensure text mode flag (-t) and error handling are complete\n   - Creating cmd/sha512sum/sha512sum_test.go with differential tests against gsha512sum\n   - Ensuring exit code semantics: 0 on success, 1 on check failures or I/O errors\n   - At least 8 differential test scenarios covering: single file, multiple files, stdin, binary mode, tag mode, check mode, missing file errors\n   - All acceptance criteria: compilation, tests pass (or skip if gsha512sum not in PATH), error handling for missing files\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: run Go binary and GNU reference binary side-by-side, compare stdout/stderr/exit code\n   - pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests, BuildBinary, DiffTest struct\n   - pkg/hashutil: DigestFiles, VerifyChecksums, HashConfig, CheckOptions, FormatGNU, FormatBSDTag\n   - SIGPIPE handling via sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n   - SHA-512 digest computation using crypto/sha512\n   - GNU checksum format: \"HASH  FILENAME\" (text) or \"HASH *FILENAME\" (binary)\n   - BSD tag format: \"SHA512 (FILENAME) = HASH\"\n   - Cobbler scaffold pipeline: measure + stitch code generation cycle\n   - No git commands allowed (orchestrator manages git)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **cmd/sha512sum/main.go** (read, to be modified)\n     - Already exists with 172 lines of complete-looking implementation\n     - Has SIGPIPE handler, flag parsing (-b, -t, --binary, --text, --tag, --check, --warn, --quiet, --status, --zero)\n     - Uses hashutil.DigestFiles and hashutil.VerifyChecksums\n     - Has nulWriter for --zero support\n     - Text mode (-t) sets opts.binary = false (already default) - R3.2 appears covered\n     - Exit codes delegated to hashutil (returns 0 or 1) - R4.1/R4.2 appear covered\n     - SIGPIPE handler called at start of main() - R4.3 covered\n     - Key code:\n     ```go\n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         opts, files := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n         cfg := hashutil.HashConfig{\n             Algorithm: \"SHA512\",\n             NewHash:   sha512.New,\n             DigestLen: 64,\n         }\n         // ... check mode and digest mode handling\n         os.Exit(hashutil.DigestFiles(files, cfg, opts.binary, opts.tag, stdout, os.Stderr))\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd033-sha512sum.yaml** (read)\n     - Full SRD covering R1 (digest computation), R2 (checksum verification), R3 (binary/text mode), R4 (exit codes/SIGPIPE)\n     - Non-goals: no HMAC-SHA512, no SHA-384 or SHA-512/256 truncations\n\n   - **pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go** (provided in project_context)\n     - DigestFiles returns int exit code (0 success, 1 on error)\n     - VerifyChecksums returns (bool, error) - bool is allOK\n     - Error messages printed to stderr by hashutil functions\n     - ParseChecksumLine handles both GNU and BSD tag formats\n\n   - **pkg/testutils/difftest.go** (provided in project_context)\n     - DiffTest struct: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n     - RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)\n     - BuildBinary(t, \".\") in pkg/testutils/build.go\n     - buildEnv sets LC_ALL=C by default\n\n   - **cmd/sha512sum/sha512sum_test.go** (to be created)\n     - Needs differential tests with at least 8 scenarios\n     - Must use testutils.BuildBinary and exec.LookPath(\"gsha512sum\")\n     - Must t.Skip if reference binary not found\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - was interrupted before implementation began\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Analyzed existing main.go and determined it already covers most requirements (R3.2, R4.1, R4.2, R4.3)\n   - The main work is creating the test file with comprehensive differential tests\n   - The main.go may need minor review but appears functionally complete\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extremely detailed task specification with full project context, SRDs, architecture, source code, execution constitution, go style guide, constraints, requirements, design decisions, acceptance criteria, and package contracts for task #5317 (sha512sum completion)\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a conversation summary\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create cmd/sha512sum/sha512sum_test.go with at least 8 differential test scenarios\n   - Review and potentially modify cmd/sha512sum/main.go if any gaps found\n   - Run `go build -o bin/sha512sum ./cmd/sha512sum/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/sha512sum/... -count=1` to verify tests pass\n   - Verify all 5 acceptance criteria (AC1-AC5)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the two key files (cmd/sha512sum/main.go and srd033-sha512sum.yaml) and was about to begin implementation. I had analyzed the existing main.go and determined it already appears to cover the required functionality (text mode flag, error handling, exit codes, SIGPIPE). The primary remaining work is creating the test file sha512sum_test.go.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Create cmd/sha512sum/sha512sum_test.go with differential tests. The test file needs:\n   - TestDiff function using testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\") and exec.LookPath(\"gsha512sum\") with t.Skip\n   - At least 8 test scenarios: single file digest, multiple files, stdin (\"-\"), binary mode (-b), tag mode (--tag), check mode (--check) with valid checksums, missing file error handling, and multiple files with one missing\n   - Each test case as a testutils.DiffTest struct with Name, Args, Stdin 