{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P2eC9LbjFB69mYpkXKYNs7","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have successfully found and read all the requested files. Here's my report:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've located and read the test file for SHA-related commands and the hashutil implementation in the go-unix-utils repository.\n\n### Test File: sha1sum_test.go\n\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5317/cmd/sha1sum/sha1sum_test.go`\n\n**Differential Testing Pattern Used:**\n\nThe test file implements a **differential testing pattern** through the `testutils.RunDiffTests()` function. The key characteristics are:\n\n1. **Reference Binary Comparison:** The test builds the Go implementation (`goBin`) and compares its output against a reference binary (`gsha1sum`), which must be installed on the system (skips if not found).\n\n2. **Test Structure:** Uses a `testutils.DiffTest` slice containing test cases with:\n   - `Name`: Test description\n   - `Args`: Command-line arguments\n   - `Stdin`: Input data\n   - `ExitCode`: Expected exit code\n   - `Normalize`: Functions to normalize output for comparison (e.g., discarding stderr)\n\n3. **Coverage Areas:**\n   - stdin handling with/without explicit \"-\"\n   - Single/multiple file hashing\n   - Binary/text mode flags\n   - Tag format output\n   - Checksum verification with `--check` flag\n   - Various failure modes (missing files, mismatched hashes, malformed checksums)\n   - Exit codes for success/failure scenarios\n   - SIGPIPE handling test\n\n### Hashutil Implementation: hashutil.go\n\n**Location:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5317/pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go`\n\n**Key Function Signatures:**\n\n1. **`DigestFiles(files []string, cfg HashConfig, binary, tag bool, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int`**\n   - Computes and prints digests for each file (or stdin)\n   - 